There can be situations where data lifecycle policy rules overlap, within or across policies. When
this happens, a rule with a more speciﬁc resource name or pattern for an index overrides a rule
with a more general resource name or pattern for any indexes that are common to both rules.
For example, in the following policy, two rules apply to an index index/sales/logstash. In this
situation, the second rule takes precedence because index/sales/log* is the longest match
to index/sales/logstash. Therefore, OpenSearch Serverless sets no retention period for the
index.
{
"Rules":[
{
"ResourceType":"index",
"Resource":[
"index/sales/*",
],
"MinIndexRetention": "15d"
},
{
"ResourceType":"index",
"Resource":[
"index/sales/log*",
],
"NoMinIndexRetention": true
}
]
}
